MiSTer Monitor — Licensing Overview
===================================

Copyright (C) 2025-2026 Adolfo Fernández (chipster6502)

MiSTer Monitor is free software, distributed under a split copyleft
license:

1. Display firmware and everything else in this repository
   (all `mister_monitor_*` folders, the web flasher, documentation and
   build tooling):

       GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at your option)
       any later version — full text in LICENSE-GPL-3.0.txt

2. MiSTer-side server (everything under `MiSTer/`, including the
   installers and `MiSTer/Scripts/.config/mister_monitor/`):

       GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 or (at your
       option) any later version — full text in LICENSE-AGPL-3.0.txt

The firmware and the server are separate programs that communicate
over HTTP. The two licenses are mutually compatible.

In short: you are free to use, study, modify and redistribute this
software — including commercially — provided that any version you
distribute (or, for the server, make available over a network) is
released under the same terms, with complete corresponding source
code.


Official pre-built binaries
---------------------------

The firmware binaries attached to GitHub releases and served through
the web flasher embed the author's private ScreenScraper developer
credentials, injected at build time from repository secrets. These
credentials are confidential material of the author and are NOT part
of the license grants above.

- You may download, flash and use the official binaries for personal
  use.
- You may NOT redistribute the official binaries in a commercial
  context (for example, selling pre-flashed devices or bundling the
  binaries with hardware for sale). Doing so would redistribute the
  private credentials and consume the project's shared ScreenScraper
  API quota.
- Commercial distribution is welcome through the source code: build
  the firmware yourself under the GPL-3.0 terms, using your own
  ScreenScraper developer credentials and your own product branding
  (see TRADEMARK.md).


Non-code assets
---------------

The licenses above apply to software. Other material in this
repository is covered as follows.

**3D-printable stands (`3d-printing/`)** — these models are NOT the
work of this project's author. They are third-party designs,
redistributed here under their own Creative Commons licenses, and the
GPL/AGPL grants above do not apply to them. Each model keeps the
license its own author chose; attribution and license details are
listed in the README's "3D-printable stand" section, and any
redistribution must preserve them. In particular, the 3.5" CYD stand
is ShareAlike, so derivatives of it must remain under the same terms.

**Screenshots, demo videos and other project media authored by this
project** — licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0). Editorial use — reviews, articles,
tutorials, videos about the project — is always welcome, including on
monetised channels. Using this media to advertise a product for sale
is a branding matter, governed by TRADEMARK.md.

**The project logo** is not covered by the CC license above; see
TRADEMARK.md.

Should this project publish original 3D models of its own in the
future, they will be licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0 and stored separately
from third-party models, with the distinction stated in the README.


Name and branding
-----------------

"MiSTer Monitor", the project logo and the official media identify
this project. The source-code licenses above do not grant any
trademark rights; see TRADEMARK.md for the branding policy, which
also describes how commercial use of the project name can be granted
in exchange for contributions back to the project.


Third-party components
----------------------

Bundled or depended-upon components keep their original licenses and
notices, including LovyanGFX (FreeBSD), M5GFX / M5Unified (MIT),
JPEGDEC (Apache-2.0), XPT2046_Touchscreen, the Arduino-ESP32 core
(LGPL-2.1 / Apache-2.0) and theypsilon's DB-Template (MIT, used by the
companion MiSTer_monitor_DB repository).


Earlier versions
----------------

Releases up to and including v2.6.0 were published under the MIT
License and remain available under those terms. The licensing
described in this file applies from the next tagged release onward.
